      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "Just deleted my own bug report about this and pasting my suggestion for a fix here instead:\n\nA manual way of designating which tracker sphere is for hip, left/right foot, maybe just pointing at and clicking each in order or something simple?\n\nLocking those bones in space relative to the tracker spheres when standing in t-pose and pulling the triggers.\n\nSince the trackers are designated for which bone to control and should just move relative to each other, it doesnt matter if you have the trackers on the side, top, front, back, whatever, of your hip or feet since the positions are still relative to each other.\n\nPossibly with an override to always use the default position for the head/hmd+hands/controllers.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
